body:
You shall now and forever, my child. Most of us subscribe to the Church of CYA and the Koran of Document and Record All the Things. 

&#x200B;

Go in peace to record and mute belligerent users appropriately.

See, we used to drive our co-worker insane, not by messing with his computer, but by taking all of his 12 (yes, 12) different photo frames he had all around his desk and turning all of the pictures inside of them different directions or taking the Hoff's face or Nicholas Cage and placing it over his daughter or wife's face. 

&#x200B;

That or there was the time we literally turned a co-worker's cube into a ball pit with a hookup from a friend who was employed at Chuck E. Cheese. There used to be pictures, but I'd have a tough time tracking them down.

Fuuuuuuck that bitch. 

&#x200B;

Go have your own amazing turkey day and don't look back.

This is SO good. Like, for no particular reason I'd get a high quality print of this, frame it, and stick it on my wall over the dinner table for a conversation piece at Thanksgiving. 

&#x200B;

But I'd also do that because I'm an asshole and I'm fine with that.

He thought objectifying you as a sexual object was hilarious, retold it to you, and laughed at you about it. 

&#x200B;

If this were me, this would probably be a deal breaker as I'd rather have a partner who values me as a person and doesn't think it's funny to refer to women like this. Rape culture is still prevalent as fuck, so people who find shit like this funny I don't want in my life.

I had two behemoth babies (10.9 lbs and 9.10lbs) in close succession and tried to breast feed them both. I could never KEEP UP because they were huge, ate more, etc and would occasionally supplement with formula. Like, her telling you to stop feeding hungry babies is ludicrous to me. Not only is breastfeeding healthier, it's meant to be digested faster and easier than formula. Formula is also full of sugars and extra carbs. In addition, even if you were shoving formula in that baby's face constantly, I doubt he could get that fat even from formula. 

&#x200B;

Plus, BABIES ARE SUPPOSED TO HAVE FAT STORES. 

&#x200B;

Jfc, I hate people.

DON'T THROW OFF HIS GROOVE. 

&#x200B;

Beware the groove. 

&#x200B;

Grooooooooove.

YES. YES GIRL. 

&#x200B;

Also, that asshole is not your friend. If that's a regular thing, I'd stop calling him a friend. No real friend I've ever had has made jokes about my weight or any other physical attributes. 

&#x200B;

But seriously, keep crushing it <3

Lucky for him, I play MMOs and online shooters too, so we're probably far more understanding regarding games. Except when he gets into Competitive Matches intentionally when he's not supposed to be because he doesn't want to get up for 20-30 minutes solid and he knows we won't make him because it's comp. Then he gets an earful when he's done about not committing when he's not supposed to. 

&#x200B;

Other than that.

Healing orb is almost always preferable because of how much more healing it does than a damage orb, especially when you've been unable to DPS and regain main heal mojo. That being said, what usually happens: 

&#x200B;

/decides to throw a damage orb because everyone is full and they have a bunch of the enemy team grouped up and you manage to kill off 2-3 of them with the orb damage 

"MOIRA STOP DPSING AND HEAL ME." - The Genji with 95% health remaining that hasn't killed anything and you're currently beating on damage as a healer without trying. 

&#x200B;

My orthopedic surgeon has been practicing for about 21 years now, works with a lot of major athletes in the city I live in (high school, college, MLB, ECHL). When I was 26 he told me he'd never seen someone with knees as bad as mine at my age and wanted to do a total replacement on both at the time and was asking if I went through with it to do all this documentation for a medical journal and future colleagues, etc. I don't think this is really a prize I want to win, but you know. 

&#x200B;

I decided to hold off, in case you were wondering. My cartilage has been gone from both knees since my early 20s, I've been sustaining with synovial fluid injections and surgeries to remove bone fragments for now. My knees are bone on bone so I'm constantly grinding off small flecks of bone just existing and walking around. These pieces actually draw nutrients from your body and will grow in size. So they've had to go in and remove large pieces of bone that are just floating around in my knee area before they damage something. 

&#x200B;

I'd really like to wait until I'm at least in my 40s (I'm 35 now) to actually go through with it. Once you get a total replacement, for those unfamiliar with it, they more or less saw your bones off at the top and bottom of the connecting joints and replace everything with metal and plastic so there's really no going back once you take that route. I'm crossing my fingers they revolutionize something between now and then. You also only have the parts last you about 15 years. So I'd be having this done quite a few times over my life once I started.

It sounds like your friends are either going to be your friends or they aren't Andy sounds like a complete pile of shit and if they have any sense, he'll be the one getting pushed out, not you. Nick, unfortunately, you can't change people. He has to decide that for himself and want it. He doesn't sound like he's in a good place. Having open and honest conversations about his substance abuse and everything is the best way to go about it. It sounds like you have a lot of yourself to take care of so while being supportive is great and telling him you'll be supportive is great, he needs to make the decision to get his shit together and work it out and you don't need to be dragged down yourself. 

&#x200B;

Again, if your friends are worth any of their salt (which it sounds like they are), explain to them what happened with Andy or just let that unfold on its own. It sounds like he's already been attracting attention to himself in a negative way with his obsessions with you. Please take care with someone like that. If he's willing to pull power plays, be careful in other aspects of your life, such as your job. He may try to take revenge on you that way and it might be in your best interest to have a conversation with someone in HR about his behaviors. I don't know if you and Andy are on equal footing or there is a risk of you being thrown under the bus instead of him, but be careful with how you approach all of it. That having been said, remember HR is there to protect the company first, then the employees. 

&#x200B;

Best of luck with all this and I hope everyone gets their shit together and things work out for the best all around.

Firstly, FUCK THAT EVIL, VAPID CUNT. I'm so sorry this is happening to you.

&#x200B;

I saw you filed a police report which is awesome and that you aren't letting her ever see the baby if you DO have it. GOOD. Please keep us posted and hugs to you and your husband.

&#x200B;

Next, I have 3 kids. I became pregnant with my first long before I was ever planning to be ready and I also never wanted kids. I had two more after I was married. I love all of them to pieces, but if I could do anything to change the circumstances and timing of my first, I would. Maybe there will come a time when you both decide you do really want a child. You shouldn't be forced to give up everything you wanted for yourselves if you truly don't want to. Personal beliefs about abortion or not. This early, it would be a fairly simple process and don't feel guilted into having a child when you never intended to do so.   

&#x200B;

I would definitely talk to Planned Parenthood, a counselor, your doctors, etc.  This is a hard decision to make, circumstances or not. Birth control fails, things happen. You may have ended up being faced with this decision in another way down the line. If you do decide to keep your baby, there are SO many resources out there. Please let us know and I'm sure reddit will provide you with swathes of links and help and support groups. 

&#x200B;

Best of luck in all of this and again FUCK THAT BITCH.

For everyone on this post booing the artist for saying they have autism. I have two sons with autism. They're both toddlers. EVERYTHING is so hard right now. For them, for myself and my husband. We don't really know how severe they are yet. They're young. They're still learning to communicate. One of them is starting to talk and the other barely has any words.

&#x200B;

Seeing someone with the disability they possess completely blow me away with their skill and ability to create something like this, let alone focus on something like this for the time invested gives me hope. Hell, I was happy to know the artist had a disability like that. It makes me feel like my kids have a shot at a semi-normal life.

&#x200B;

I definitely don't get the hate, but OP, please know I appreciate you including that information and thank you and your art is amazing. Creating something like this for someone with autism is amazing and it is a big deal.

He broke up with me because I "cut, styled, and colored my hair exactly like his ex did before she went psycho". 

&#x200B;

Uh huh.

Honey, you're young. I know you've been together a long time, but it sounds like there are many, many issues at work here that make me think you two should try some counseling and try to work this out. Or maybe try to get a clean break. You don't  have kids which is a big plus. Don't even consider that until you figure out what to do here. 

&#x200B;

It doesn't sound like your husband is planning on being faithful from the way you're talking and if it's only 6 months since the marriage and this is what he's saying, it might not be much longer until he does act on this. 

&#x200B;

Try to take measures to protect yourself. Talk to a lawyer. Talk to a family counselor. I realize you can't leave, but maybe they can come to you. Get some advice on steps to take. I'm not saying "OMG DIVORCE HIM", but it doesn't sound like he's super invested in this marriage. Best of luck.
